*How much to write: 4 points · 3 minutes*

Genetic modification has (any four):
1. made crops <mark>more tolerant to abiotic stresses</mark> (cold, drought, salt, heat);
2. <mark>reduced reliance on chemical pesticides</mark> (pest-resistant crops such as Bt cotton);
3. helped to <u>reduce post-harvest losses</u>;
4. <u>increased efficiency of mineral usage</u> by plants (prevents early exhaustion of soil fertility);
5. <u>enhanced nutritional value</u> of food, e.g. <u>Golden rice</u>, rich in vitamin A.

:::tip Your answer must contain
- four distinct advantages
- an example such as <u>Bt cotton</u> or <u>Golden rice</u> helps
:::

**Marks are lost for:** repeating the same advantage in different words; listing disadvantages.
